posts.body:
If you do it like the above poster suggested, many of the users here will s*** on your game. So here's an alternative suggestion:
Didn't test it, but can you modify the text you feed it in the below function. Let's say you have a game variable made into an array where you store your kill counts per enemyId [5, 2, 0, 4, ...]. Then another variable array where you store texts per enemy id. Then you can check:
if ($gameVariables.value(X)[enemy.id] > Y)
change the drawEncyclopediaMeta function to draw
enemy.meta.cgmvdesc + $gameVariables.value(Z)[enemy.id]
CGMV_Window_EncyclopediaDisplay.prototype.drawBestiary = function() {
var enemy = $dataEnemies[this._data._id];
this.drawEncyclopediaName(enemy.name);
this.drawEncyclopediaStats(enemy.params, this.lineHeight());
this.drawEncyclopediaCenteredText(CGMV.Encyclopedia.DropsText, this.lineHeight()*5, true);
this.drawEncyclopediaBestiaryRewards(enemy.exp, enemy.gold);
var y = this.drawEncyclopediaBestiaryDrops(enemy.dropItems);
y = this.drawEncyclopediaMeta(enemy.meta.cgmvdesc, y);
y = this.drawEncyclopediaBestiarySketch(enemy.battlerHue, enemy.battlerName, y);
this._neededHeight = y;
};
